{{also|schaden}}
==German==

===Alternative form===
* {{l/de|Schade}} {{i|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|scado|lang=goh}}. Confer {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|schade|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|scathe|lang=en}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|skada|lang=sv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃaːdən/|[ˈʃaːdən]|[ˈʃaːdn̩]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-schaden.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Schadens|Schäden}}

# [[damage]]
#: ''Das Gehäuse hat einen '''Schaden'''.'' - The case is damaged.
# [[harm]]
#: ''Ich möchte ihm keinen '''Schaden''' zufügen.'' - I don't want to harm him.
# (einen Schaden haben) (colloquial, derogative): to be [[mentally]] [[deficient]]

====Declension====
